# VOLTA Infostealer - Suricata Rules
# Reference: https://blog.talosintelligence.com/appraisal-by-ai-model-driven-victim-prioritization-in-the-volta-infostealer/
# Author: Actioner CTI
# Date: 2026-11-07
# NOTE: All HTTP-content rules require TLS inspection; VOLTA exfils to Telegram over HTTPS.
# Without TLS inspection, only DNS-based detection applies (none retained -- see revision notes).
# revision: dropped SID 2026110801 (generic OpenRouter API detection -- not VOLTA-specific)
# revision: dropped SID 2026110802 (LLM model string -- not VOLTA-exclusive)
# revision: dropped SID 2026110804 (bare DNS query to legitimate service; misclassified as trojan-activity)

# Rule 1: Detect VOLTA archive filename in HTTP upload
alert http $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET any (msg:"Actioner - VOLTA Exfiltration Archive volta_dox.zip in Upload"; flow:established,to_server; http.method; content:"POST"; http.request_body; content:"volta_dox.zip"; nocase; classtype:trojan-activity; sid:2026110803; rev:1; metadata: author Actioner, created_at 2026-11-07;)

# Rule 2: Detect VOLTA staged exfil archive volta_log.zip
alert http $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET any (msg:"Actioner - VOLTA Staged Exfil Archive volta_log.zip"; flow:established,to_server; http.method; content:"POST"; http.request_body; content:"volta_log.zip"; nocase; classtype:trojan-activity; sid:2026110805; rev:1; metadata: author Actioner, created_at 2026-11-07;)
